1
00:00:08,441 --> 00:00:10,944
CLINIC

2
00:00:42,008 --> 00:00:44,244
- Cosmetic surgery?
- That's different.

3
00:00:44,677 --> 00:00:46,546
But, you guys...

4
00:00:46,613 --> 00:00:49,816
- ... don't need it!
- Really?

5
00:00:50,116 --> 00:00:52,685
Dr. Morimoto,
what kind of doctor are you?

6
00:00:53,853 --> 00:00:54,921
Surgeon.

7
00:00:54,988 --> 00:00:57,924
Surgeon? Did you open anyone up today?

8
00:00:58,825 --> 00:00:59,659
- Yeah.
- Ew!

9
00:00:59,726 --> 00:01:01,961
HIKARU MORIMOTO - TOTEI UNIVERSITY
THIRD HOSPITAL #2 SURGERY ASSISTANT

10
00:01:02,028 --> 00:01:03,196
Okay, I'm going.

11
00:01:04,664 --> 00:01:05,799
Morimoto!

12
00:01:06,332 --> 00:01:09,903
It's all good.
We're just getting started, right?

13
00:01:10,503 --> 00:01:12,338
I'm tired and have to wake up
at 5:00 tomorrow.

14
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:13,573
Don't be a downer!

15
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:15,208
I'm just here to show up.

16
00:01:29,222 --> 00:01:30,390
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

17
00:01:31,391 --> 00:01:32,725
- Thanks for everything.
- What do you mean?

18
00:01:32,826 --> 00:01:33,993
KANEKO TERAYAMA
TOTEI UNIVERSITY THIRD HOSPITAL MANAGER

19
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:35,061
We're going out.

20
00:01:35,195 --> 00:01:36,262
Thanks for your help.

21
00:01:36,362 --> 00:01:39,032
Wait a minute!
You quit suddenly without saying anything!

22
00:01:41,134 --> 00:01:43,369
Let's talk. I want to hear your terms.

23
00:01:45,872 --> 00:01:46,873
RESERVED TODAY - TOTEI UNIVERSITY
HOSPITAL FACULTY ASSOCIATION

24
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:49,709
What exactly is
the Health Ministry thinking of?

25
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:57,484
The introduction of the post-graduate
doctor system in 2004 was a huge failure.

26
00:01:57,550 --> 00:01:59,085
RYUNOSUKE BUSUJIMA
TOTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL PROFESSOR

27
00:01:59,152 --> 00:02:01,287
Without devoted medical officers,

28
00:02:01,421 --> 00:02:04,591
the university hospital's medicine
will be of no use.

29
00:02:09,729 --> 00:02:12,098
They don't get that the destruction
of the medical office

30
00:02:12,198 --> 00:02:14,067
is the destruction of medicine in Japan.

31
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:15,335
TAKASHI TORII - TOTEI UNIVERSITY THIRD
HOSPITAL - 2ND SURGERY HEAD/PROFESSOR

32
00:02:15,401 --> 00:02:16,402
That's right.

33
00:02:16,469 --> 00:02:19,005
What about the race
for the Main Hospital Chief position?

34
00:02:19,072 --> 00:02:20,073
SHIGERU KUBO
TOTEI UNIVERSITY THIRD HOSPITAL CHIEF

35
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:23,443
Hard to say. That's
Professor Busujima's decision, right?

36
00:02:23,510 --> 00:02:25,645
No, I don't know yet.

37
00:02:26,112 --> 00:02:27,881
The election is a thing of chance.

38
00:02:28,114 --> 00:02:30,650
I'll ask for your consensus in advance.

39
00:02:36,189 --> 00:02:40,026
Dr. Kubo, you've been Third Hospital Chief
for a long time, right?

40
00:02:40,627 --> 00:02:44,297
Isn't it about time
you come back to the main campus?

41
00:02:44,631 --> 00:02:47,467
I would really like that.

42
00:02:49,402 --> 00:02:51,237
For a new chief...

43
00:02:51,871 --> 00:02:53,640
I think Professor Torii is good.

44
00:02:57,977 --> 00:03:00,013
No, I'm not ready yet.

45
00:03:04,083 --> 00:03:05,151
Please.

46
00:03:08,454 --> 00:03:09,889
Sorry, please excuse me.

47
00:03:10,356 --> 00:03:11,824
He's fixed to his phone!

48
00:03:12,992 --> 00:03:15,862
Hello, what is it?
I'm in an important meeting.

49
00:03:15,929 --> 00:03:16,896
Professor Torii, this is bad!

50
00:03:16,963 --> 00:03:17,797
#2 SURGERY OFFICE

51
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:21,234
Dr. Asano, Dr. Ishida and Dr. Kimura
from #2 Surgery,

52
00:03:21,935 --> 00:03:22,902
they all quit!

53
00:03:22,969 --> 00:03:23,870
What?

54
00:03:26,372 --> 00:03:28,675
All at once? How foolish.

55
00:03:29,075 --> 00:03:30,276
Hey, that's enough.

56
00:03:31,177 --> 00:03:32,345
Let me through.

57
00:03:33,746 --> 00:03:34,814
Sir, are you okay?

58
00:03:34,881 --> 00:03:37,150
- Call the ambulance quick!
- Yes!

59
00:03:38,251 --> 00:03:39,085
Stop it.

60
00:03:39,352 --> 00:03:41,988
Don't lend a hand. What if you get sued?

61
00:03:49,195 --> 00:03:51,898
Excuse me, please let me through! Sorry.

62
00:03:53,866 --> 00:03:54,701
Are you okay?

63
00:03:54,867 --> 00:03:56,236
- Are you a doctor?
- Yes.

64
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:04,143
Does it hurt here?

65
00:04:17,323 --> 00:04:18,191
Hey, you.

66
00:04:21,894 --> 00:04:23,730
You do that, he's going to die.

67
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:27,834
Support him in the back, stand him up.

68
00:04:28,067 --> 00:04:28,901
Hey.

69
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:31,104
Yes.

70
00:04:41,981 --> 00:04:43,483
What are you doing?

71
00:04:51,724 --> 00:04:54,294
He has a strong pain
in the right groin region.

72
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:56,496
It seems like a strangulated hernia,
I think it can be treated.

73
00:04:56,562 --> 00:04:58,698
STRANGULATED HERNIA - A HERNIA THAT
DOESN'T GO AWAY, TREATMENT IS NECESSARY

74
00:04:58,765 --> 00:05:01,467
- No way, are you a doctor?
- Manual reposition is impossible.

75
00:05:01,701 --> 00:05:04,637
Muscular defense in the abdominal walls,
the digestive tract has been constricted.

76
00:05:04,704 --> 00:05:06,105
He needs emergency surgery.

77
00:05:06,172 --> 00:05:07,974
You're a doctor? Please ride with us.

78
00:05:08,041 --> 00:05:10,643
- Ride with him. You're a doctor, right?
- Huh?

79
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:13,313
Ow!

80
00:05:14,013 --> 00:05:15,515
- Closing the door!
- Wait!

81
00:05:15,982 --> 00:05:17,283
Who are you?

82
00:05:19,485 --> 00:05:21,788
A dancer passing by!

83
00:05:21,854 --> 00:05:23,289
- Huh?
- Closing!

84
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:47,046
<i>2012.</i>

85
00:05:47,113 --> 00:05:47,947
TEITO MEDICAL UNIVERSITY THIRD HOSPITAL

86
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:48,948
<i>This white building</i>

87
00:05:49,482 --> 00:05:52,085
<i>seems like it is on the verge of collapse.</i>

88
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:55,121
- Where's Dr. Asano? What?
- He quit.

89
00:05:56,356 --> 00:05:59,025
<i>Medicine in university hospitals</i>
<i>has weakened,</i>

90
00:05:59,359 --> 00:06:01,861
<i>and the doctors' hierarchy</i>
<i>has been broken.</i>

91
00:06:02,495 --> 00:06:04,630
<i>Medicine, which deals in human life,</i>

92
00:06:04,931 --> 00:06:08,701
<i>has finally come to the era</i>
<i>of the law of the jungle.</i>

93
00:06:10,603 --> 00:06:12,572
<i>The once thriving surgery department</i>

94
00:06:12,638 --> 00:06:15,875
<i>has suddenly changed</i>
<i>due to harsh working conditions.</i>

95
00:06:15,942 --> 00:06:17,777
#2 SURGERY TEACHER
HIDEKI KAJI

96
00:06:17,844 --> 00:06:20,146
<i>There are also many medical offices</i>
<i>that are getting worse.</i>

97
00:06:20,213 --> 00:06:21,481
#2 SURGERY ASSISTANT PROFESSOR
MAMORU HARA

98
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:25,451
Asano and Ishida got
three times as much at the Mayo Clinic.

99
00:06:25,685 --> 00:06:27,120
Seems like headhunting.

100
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:29,389
Hmm. How about Kimura?

101
00:06:29,756 --> 00:06:33,259
His wife's family has a private practice,
so I think he's taking it over.

102
00:06:33,326 --> 00:06:34,293
I see.

103
00:06:34,927 --> 00:06:38,264
He'll probably be making five times more
than at a university hospital.

104
00:06:38,698 --> 00:06:39,866
I made it!

105
00:06:40,266 --> 00:06:42,735
But why did those three quit so suddenly?

106
00:06:43,035 --> 00:06:43,936
Morimoto!

107
00:06:44,737 --> 00:06:46,406
What are the six Ks of surgery?

108
00:06:47,039 --> 00:06:48,641
<i>Kitsui, Kitanai, Kiken.</i>

109
00:06:48,708 --> 00:06:51,477
I remember those three,
what are the others?

110
00:06:51,811 --> 00:06:54,514
<i>Koshi warui, Kakko warui,</i>
<i>Kyuuryou yasui.</i>

111
00:06:55,047 --> 00:06:57,884
You should quit
and take over your family clinic.

112
00:06:58,050 --> 00:07:02,021
I don't want to. Now that they quit,
I am next in line for operations.

113
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:04,190
Third assistants just need to suction.

114
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:05,324
HIROMI JONOUCHI
ANESTHESIOLOGIST

115
00:07:10,963 --> 00:07:13,166
How many operations do we have today?

116
00:07:14,033 --> 00:07:15,802
Where did Dr. Torii go?

117
00:07:16,569 --> 00:07:18,137
This is a problem.

118
00:07:18,738 --> 00:07:21,541
I humbly apologize.
We should have seen this, but...

119
00:07:21,607 --> 00:07:25,278
However, surgery is short people.
What are you going to do?

120
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:27,313
Manager?

121
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:29,749
Yes. Everything is okay.

122
00:07:30,416 --> 00:07:34,253
We already found one person
who will do the work of three people.

123
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:43,362
<i>In a medical area</i>
<i>where no one wants to come,</i>

124
00:07:43,763 --> 00:07:47,967
<i>a completely new type of doctor</i>
<i>has arrived.</i>

125
00:08:00,746 --> 00:08:03,749
- Thank you very much.
- Thank you very much.

126
00:08:06,052 --> 00:08:11,724
<i>From now, #2 Surgery shall do</i>
<i>the rounds with Hospital Chief, Dr. Kubo.</i>

127
00:08:13,125 --> 00:08:18,064
<i>There are two types of doctors:</i>
<i>those in hospitals and practitioners.</i>

128
00:08:19,065 --> 00:08:20,867
<i>Most doctors in hospitals</i>

129
00:08:20,933 --> 00:08:24,537
<i>have been hired by personnel</i>
<i>in the university hospital.</i>

130
00:08:24,604 --> 00:08:27,940
<i>Then there are those who don't belong</i>
<i>to a university hospital... freelance.</i>

131
00:08:28,774 --> 00:08:29,675
<i>In other words,</i>

132
00:08:30,009 --> 00:08:33,212
<i>one of these freelance doctors</i>
<i>has appeared.</i>

133
00:08:34,814 --> 00:08:36,415
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

134
00:08:37,383 --> 00:08:39,919
<i>She hates groups, she hates authority,</i>

135
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:41,821
<i>and she hates restraints.</i>

136
00:08:42,855 --> 00:08:48,327
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

137
00:09:15,254 --> 00:09:16,923
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

138
00:09:17,957 --> 00:09:18,824
<i>Also known as...</i>

139
00:09:20,393 --> 00:09:21,761
<i>Doctor X.</i>

140
00:09:30,803 --> 00:09:33,906
DOCTOR X SURGEON MICHIKO DAIMON
EPISODE 1

141
00:09:33,973 --> 00:09:36,108
#2 SURGERY PROFESSOR'S ROOM
TAKASHI TORII

142
00:09:39,011 --> 00:09:42,682
The professor is away from his desk,
but what are you here for?

143
00:09:45,318 --> 00:09:49,555
You... What's your relation to Dr. Torii?

144
00:09:49,622 --> 00:09:50,890
Why?

145
00:09:50,957 --> 00:09:51,924
AI OKUMURA
DR. TORII'S SECRETARY

146
00:09:51,991 --> 00:09:52,825
That bag.

147
00:09:52,892 --> 00:09:55,728
- Who bought that for you?
- Again, why?

148
00:10:03,235 --> 00:10:04,136
Who's this?

149
00:10:04,870 --> 00:10:08,107
I want to hear... this woman, who is she?

150
00:10:11,310 --> 00:10:13,746
- I've seen her somewhere before.
- Doctor!

151
00:10:16,749 --> 00:10:17,883
I'm Michiko Daimon.

152
00:10:19,218 --> 00:10:20,052
A new hire?

153
00:10:24,890 --> 00:10:25,725
That's you?

154
00:10:26,692 --> 00:10:27,526
Yes.

155
00:10:31,964 --> 00:10:32,798
Excuse me.

156
00:10:34,066 --> 00:10:34,900
Professor.

157
00:10:36,168 --> 00:10:37,937
It's time for the conference.

158
00:10:38,004 --> 00:10:40,006
Got it. You come, too.

159
00:10:40,873 --> 00:10:43,676
Wear a white gown.
Okumura, get one for her.

160
00:10:44,443 --> 00:10:45,277
Okay.

161
00:10:57,089 --> 00:10:59,158
PRE-OPERATION CONFERENCE

162
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:05,297
Okay. We'll begin
this week's pre-operation conference.

163
00:11:06,132 --> 00:11:10,603
As we confirmed last time, we have
three operations planned for tomorrow.

164
00:11:11,570 --> 00:11:13,439
Who is that strange woman?

165
00:11:13,773 --> 00:11:16,509
The surgeon to help replace
the three who quit.

166
00:11:16,575 --> 00:11:18,911
- Where did they find her?
- Well...

167
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:22,181
She seems strange.

168
00:11:23,149 --> 00:11:24,717
I've met her before.

169
00:11:25,651 --> 00:11:26,519
Where?

170
00:11:27,353 --> 00:11:28,487
I don't remember.

171
00:11:34,393 --> 00:11:36,595
A dancer passing by!

172
00:11:37,296 --> 00:11:38,130
What?

173
00:11:38,597 --> 00:11:40,132
A dancer passing by!

174
00:11:41,133 --> 00:11:46,105
Morimoto, a dancer passing by...
Are you getting enough sleep?

175
00:11:46,706 --> 00:11:48,307
Sounds pretty severe.

176
00:11:56,449 --> 00:12:00,486
The first operation is to remove
a gallstone, 60-year-old Jiro Ichinose.

177
00:12:00,553 --> 00:12:03,355
Cholecystectomy is through
an abdominal section.

178
00:12:03,422 --> 00:12:08,794
The patient's strong request is
that Chief Kubo participate himself.

179
00:12:11,330 --> 00:12:15,801
What's more is that this was developed by
Dr. Kubo 30 years ago, the Kubo technique.

180
00:12:17,670 --> 00:12:21,741
What is this Kubo technique?
It's just an abdominal section.

181
00:12:21,807 --> 00:12:26,011
This is a simple operation.
For the first assistant, I see...

182
00:12:26,078 --> 00:12:28,948
Morimoto. Come with me for experience.

183
00:12:30,449 --> 00:12:32,752
- Yes!
- That's good, Morimoto.

184
00:12:33,352 --> 00:12:37,456
Yes. Observing Dr. Kubo do his work
gives me inspiration.

185
00:12:38,224 --> 00:12:41,427
Anyone who is still free,
please come and observe.

186
00:12:41,494 --> 00:12:43,129
Good. I will come.

187
00:12:43,529 --> 00:12:44,630
- Good.
- Good.

188
00:12:46,632 --> 00:12:47,700
I object.

189
00:13:01,914 --> 00:13:02,815
This...

190
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:06,385
Does he have to have an abdominal section?

191
00:13:08,087 --> 00:13:10,689
Instead of having
this amateur cut him open,

192
00:13:10,856 --> 00:13:13,125
shouldn't we have a decent surgeon?

193
00:13:14,627 --> 00:13:17,363
If it's a gallstone,
laparoscopic surgery can get it easily.

194
00:13:17,429 --> 00:13:18,430
LAPAROSCOPIC SURGERY

195
00:13:18,497 --> 00:13:22,101
There will be fewer wounds, less pain
and he'll be out in two to three days.

196
00:13:22,868 --> 00:13:25,838
An abdominal section will take
more than ten days in the hospital.

197
00:13:26,338 --> 00:13:28,541
The damage after the operation
is also great.

198
00:13:29,175 --> 00:13:31,844
Even so you want to cut the patient open?

199
00:13:31,911 --> 00:13:34,814
You! Why are you so rude as a new hire?

200
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:36,182
It's okay, Manager.

201
00:13:39,952 --> 00:13:42,221
You're the new surgeon, right?

202
00:13:43,222 --> 00:13:47,293
Young ones always jump at
the first chance to say something.

203
00:13:49,528 --> 00:13:51,197
Large things such as wounds

204
00:13:51,864 --> 00:13:54,834
should not be feared by surgeons.

205
00:13:56,669 --> 00:14:01,106
For an abdominal section,
you look at the whole operative field,

206
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:06,212
and if you touch something,
any hemostasis can be handled with fusion.

207
00:14:07,079 --> 00:14:08,881
We think of safety first.

208
00:14:10,649 --> 00:14:11,483
Chief.

209
00:14:12,551 --> 00:14:17,089
It's been a long time since you operated.
Don't you just want to cut him open?

210
00:14:21,627 --> 00:14:25,431
Isn't it better to change to a doctor
who can perform a laparoscopic surgery?

211
00:14:32,271 --> 00:14:33,739
So, shall I do it?

212
00:14:34,907 --> 00:14:35,875
Get out of here!

213
00:14:38,143 --> 00:14:39,011
Hey!

214
00:14:39,378 --> 00:14:40,746
Get out! Hurry!

215
00:14:40,946 --> 00:14:43,515
Hey, out! Out!

216
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:53,926
That a world-class hospital
would let a freeter in...

217
00:14:54,727 --> 00:14:56,929
The manager was really impatient.

218
00:14:57,396 --> 00:14:58,931
Blood loss is over 400.

219
00:14:59,798 --> 00:15:01,901
Freeter, I said! Freeter!

220
00:15:02,201 --> 00:15:03,769
- Sweat.
- Okay!

221
00:15:04,436 --> 00:15:06,772
Oh, really? This is tough.

222
00:15:08,007 --> 00:15:10,743
She had no idea
of how to read a situation.

223
00:15:10,876 --> 00:15:11,977
- Really?
- Yeah.

224
00:15:12,444 --> 00:15:14,513
- Manager?
- Huh?

225
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:17,216
I'm on with Dr. Kambara,
who introduced her.

226
00:15:17,283 --> 00:15:18,117
Okay.

227
00:15:20,419 --> 00:15:22,421
Hello? Dr. Kambara?

228
00:15:23,255 --> 00:15:25,958
I've known you for a very long time,

229
00:15:26,492 --> 00:15:30,996
but what the hell was with
that rude woman you gave us? Huh?

230
00:15:31,730 --> 00:15:33,966
Eh? Daimon was rude?

231
00:15:34,033 --> 00:15:34,934
DOCTOR REFERRAL
KAMBARA

232
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,769
Hiring? Yes.

233
00:15:36,835 --> 00:15:38,604
I understand your anger.

234
00:15:39,104 --> 00:15:41,106
She can be blunt, but she has ability.

235
00:15:41,573 --> 00:15:43,242
I think she can be useful.

236
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:47,913
Try her with a one-month contract
and you can renegotiate after that.

237
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:49,248
AKIRA KAMBARA
DOCTOR REFERRAL SERVICE CHIEF

238
00:15:49,315 --> 00:15:50,883
I think you should try her out.

239
00:15:51,050 --> 00:15:53,052
Yeah. Well then, okay.

240
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:55,387
Sorry, she was so noisy.

241
00:15:55,521 --> 00:15:58,424
You're hungry, right?
Let's get you some food.

242
00:15:58,490 --> 00:16:03,862
Is it true, your most elite surgeon,
Dr. Kubo, will come?

243
00:16:04,330 --> 00:16:06,865
Yes.
The Hospital Chief will do it himself.

244
00:16:08,567 --> 00:16:12,471
To think that the University
Hospital Chief would do my surgery,

245
00:16:13,038 --> 00:16:16,041
to get that much
feels like a dream come true!

246
00:16:16,375 --> 00:16:18,777
Honey, we're really lucky!

247
00:16:19,244 --> 00:16:21,280
Well then, please sign this form.

248
00:16:21,413 --> 00:16:22,414
Ah, okay.

249
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:27,086
JIRO ICHINOSE

250
00:16:27,553 --> 00:16:30,723
Um, this isn't very interesting, but...

251
00:16:30,856 --> 00:16:33,492
It's our policy not to accept gifts.

252
00:16:33,559 --> 00:16:37,129
- I'm not sure if you'll like it or not.
- Please don't worry.

253
00:16:37,429 --> 00:16:38,964
Please, enjoy these!

254
00:16:39,031 --> 00:16:41,800
Really, it's really all right.

255
00:17:07,559 --> 00:17:09,294
- Morimoto.
- Yes?

256
00:17:09,495 --> 00:17:11,163
Take this to the medical office.

257
00:17:11,563 --> 00:17:13,098
Yes. Thank you very much.

258
00:17:14,566 --> 00:17:17,236
Professor, this is
the operation consent form.

259
00:17:22,808 --> 00:17:26,045
Professor, this is the resume
from the referral office.

260
00:17:26,445 --> 00:17:27,279
Read it.

261
00:17:29,014 --> 00:17:30,115
"Michiko Daimon.

262
00:17:30,616 --> 00:17:32,918
Graduated from
the Meiei Medical School in 2001.

263
00:17:32,985 --> 00:17:35,854
Entered and left the Totei
University Hospital surgical department.

264
00:17:35,921 --> 00:17:39,124
Transferred to the Cubanacan
Medical School in Cuba in 2002.

265
00:17:39,191 --> 00:17:40,526
Worked in a remote clinic after,

266
00:17:40,626 --> 00:17:42,828
then as an army and ship doctor
and came back to Japan."

267
00:17:43,429 --> 00:17:44,296
Really?

268
00:17:44,363 --> 00:17:48,200
"Registered with the Kambara
Referral Office as a freelancer surgeon.

269
00:17:48,667 --> 00:17:51,503
Her special skill is surgery.
Her hobby: surgery."

270
00:17:52,371 --> 00:17:53,272
What is that?

271
00:17:54,873 --> 00:17:57,209
- You called me?
- Yes.

272
00:17:57,810 --> 00:18:00,813
You'll be helping Morimoto with his work.

273
00:18:01,113 --> 00:18:01,947
Huh?

274
00:18:02,347 --> 00:18:05,084
With things like filing medical records
and getting conference material.

275
00:18:06,718 --> 00:18:07,586
Answer me.

276
00:18:07,719 --> 00:18:11,023
I can do that
without a medical license, yes?

277
00:18:13,358 --> 00:18:14,793
So, what?

278
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:15,994
So why?

279
00:18:17,663 --> 00:18:18,931
Enough. Hurry and go.

280
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:27,139
Excuse me.

281
00:18:43,989 --> 00:18:46,859
It seems like a strangulated hernia,
I think it can be treated.

282
00:18:46,925 --> 00:18:48,260
Emergency surgery may be needed.

283
00:18:51,930 --> 00:18:53,832
Um, thanks for the other day.

284
00:18:55,501 --> 00:18:58,036
The patient that was taken
in the ambulance,

285
00:18:58,103 --> 00:19:00,772
he had a strangulated hernia
as you diagnosed.

286
00:19:02,274 --> 00:19:05,944
It wasn't life-threatening
because you came there.

287
00:19:07,212 --> 00:19:10,883
I can imagine your career as an army
and ship doctor has been different.

288
00:19:13,819 --> 00:19:17,189
But... why did you dance at the club?

289
00:19:19,224 --> 00:19:21,793
I mistook you for someone else.

290
00:19:23,095 --> 00:19:25,898
Um, is there anything you can say?

291
00:19:27,032 --> 00:19:27,866
I'll say it.

292
00:19:28,967 --> 00:19:33,872
Taking part in your stupid conversation
doesn't require a medical license.

293
00:19:35,908 --> 00:19:37,643
So what's your point?

294
00:19:40,445 --> 00:19:41,747
Don't talk to me.

295
00:19:52,257 --> 00:19:54,059
NAME: JIRO ICHINOSE
AGE: 60

296
00:19:56,295 --> 00:19:58,030
COMPANY NAME: ICHINOSE RUBBER

297
00:20:03,735 --> 00:20:05,938
Mr. Ichinose,
he's having the operation tomorrow.

298
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:08,173
He's the president of a tiny company.

299
00:20:08,507 --> 00:20:11,510
He's responsible for running the factory,

300
00:20:11,977 --> 00:20:14,479
and I understand why he wants
to rely on the Chief.

301
00:20:14,546 --> 00:20:15,480
Then I'll ask you,

302
00:20:16,014 --> 00:20:19,318
if you were the patient,
would you let the Chief cut you open?

303
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:24,156
His title doesn't matter.

304
00:20:36,468 --> 00:20:37,536
What are you doing?

305
00:20:38,036 --> 00:20:40,672
Now, now, let it go.

306
00:20:47,212 --> 00:20:49,214
It's time, so please excuse me.

307
00:20:49,881 --> 00:20:52,417
Hey, there's a limit
to how rude you can be!

308
00:20:56,989 --> 00:20:59,891
A very elite doctor
will be doing my surgery!

309
00:20:59,958 --> 00:21:02,427
Yeah, don't worry! Later.

310
00:21:11,970 --> 00:21:14,940
Are you hospital staff?
Sorry, I'm just having one.

311
00:21:15,507 --> 00:21:16,341
Go ahead.

312
00:21:17,009 --> 00:21:18,844
I have an operation tomorrow.

313
00:21:19,378 --> 00:21:23,015
Since I'm going under anesthesia,
this might be my last one, right?

314
00:21:24,983 --> 00:21:27,719
How long have you run your factory?

315
00:21:28,587 --> 00:21:31,156
Since I first founded it, about 40 years.

316
00:21:32,357 --> 00:21:33,191
Is that long?

317
00:21:34,693 --> 00:21:36,895
Why bother with the surgery?

318
00:21:36,962 --> 00:21:37,796
Huh?

319
00:21:38,664 --> 00:21:39,931
You can put it off.

320
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:43,902
- Are you a doctor?
- Yes.

321
00:21:45,570 --> 00:21:47,939
I don't have gallstones?

322
00:21:48,807 --> 00:21:51,543
I heard they are so severe
that I need surgery!

323
00:21:51,610 --> 00:21:53,312
No, they're gallstones.

324
00:21:53,378 --> 00:21:55,247
Don't say strange things!

325
00:21:55,914 --> 00:21:57,482
An elite doctor came

326
00:21:58,116 --> 00:22:01,153
and said if I didn't take care of this,
my factory would go under!

327
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:17,002
FEROCIOUS CAT
DON'T TOUCH WITHOUT PERMISSION

328
00:22:17,069 --> 00:22:19,004
BEN CASEY

329
00:22:22,507 --> 00:22:25,711
Michiko, you haven't paid
your portion this month yet.

330
00:22:29,948 --> 00:22:31,049
Right now...

331
00:22:32,417 --> 00:22:33,352
I just have this.

332
00:22:34,286 --> 00:22:35,554
Once I have a contract, I'll give it back.

333
00:22:35,620 --> 00:22:36,521
Michiko...

334
00:22:36,955 --> 00:22:40,225
I got a call right away to get rid of you.
Read between the lines.

335
00:22:43,261 --> 00:22:45,630
Mi-chan. How's your new workplace?

336
00:22:46,098 --> 00:22:48,266
It's a typical ivory tower.

337
00:22:48,533 --> 00:22:51,436
Teito Medical College is
a colony of Totei University.

338
00:22:51,570 --> 00:22:53,872
All of the doctors' posts
at Totei University

339
00:22:53,939 --> 00:22:55,574
are controlled by professors.

340
00:22:56,007 --> 00:23:00,045
The Third Hospital is
a branch office, like a colony,

341
00:23:00,579 --> 00:23:02,280
so the professors there are frantic.

342
00:23:02,347 --> 00:23:04,950
If they get thrown farther out,
they don't come back.

343
00:23:05,050 --> 00:23:06,017
Right.

344
00:23:07,319 --> 00:23:10,055
By the way, Dr. Kubo there,
is he doing well?

345
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:12,858
Akira, you know Chief Kubo?

346
00:23:12,958 --> 00:23:16,461
I used to play mah-jong with him.
But he's done, too old!

347
00:23:17,295 --> 00:23:19,564
He dropped tiles and his hands shake.

348
00:23:20,832 --> 00:23:22,267
Well, I saw his blog.

349
00:23:22,334 --> 00:23:25,237
<i>He has marbled steak</i>
<i>and red wine every day.</i>

350
00:23:25,303 --> 00:23:28,273
- Meat lover!
- Even though he's old.

351
00:23:28,707 --> 00:23:30,909
The surgical professor is energetic,

352
00:23:30,976 --> 00:23:32,677
but his blood vessels are messed up.

353
00:23:32,744 --> 00:23:34,746
His blood vessels are messed up?

354
00:23:35,213 --> 00:23:37,215
If he keeps up that lifestyle,

355
00:23:37,349 --> 00:23:39,351
he'll surely pay. <i>Riichi!</i>

356
00:23:39,451 --> 00:23:40,385
<i>Ron!</i>

357
00:23:44,623 --> 00:23:45,957
Didn't I get that one?

358
00:23:47,192 --> 00:23:49,294
His blood vessels are messed up...

359
00:23:51,630 --> 00:23:54,966
- You say this suddenly, but...
- Give the invoice to the manager.

360
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:56,868
To the manager? I can't do that!

361
00:23:56,935 --> 00:23:58,270
Doctor!

362
00:23:58,837 --> 00:24:00,939
- Professor Torii is--
- That woman.

363
00:24:02,207 --> 00:24:04,743
We have to keep an eye on her.

364
00:24:06,478 --> 00:24:08,847
She stuck to the contractor immediately,

365
00:24:10,449 --> 00:24:12,217
trying to get money.

366
00:24:13,485 --> 00:24:14,486
No way.

367
00:24:15,787 --> 00:24:17,255
Ah, the professor is coming.

368
00:24:20,625 --> 00:24:21,693
I think you know,

369
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:24,496
- but help the Chief at all costs.
- Yes.

370
00:24:25,397 --> 00:24:28,233
It's been a while
since the Chief was in surgery.

371
00:24:28,834 --> 00:24:30,435
This is a heavy duty for him.

372
00:24:30,502 --> 00:24:32,671
Understood. I'll take care of what I can.

373
00:24:32,737 --> 00:24:35,841
Please do.
Morimoto isn't enough to help him.

374
00:24:36,241 --> 00:24:39,277
Follow Hara without the Chief noticing.

375
00:24:39,344 --> 00:24:40,712
- Understood.
- And...

376
00:24:40,779 --> 00:24:42,280
- Huh?
- And...

377
00:24:43,014 --> 00:24:45,150
I will make sure
not to wound the Chief's pride.

378
00:24:45,283 --> 00:24:46,418
Do your best!

379
00:24:47,919 --> 00:24:49,221
You surprised me!

380
00:24:49,287 --> 00:24:51,857
- What are you...
- Why so suddenly?

381
00:24:53,859 --> 00:24:54,893
What is it, Daimon?

382
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:56,795
Please let me attend the operation.

383
00:24:57,362 --> 00:24:58,196
Why?

384
00:24:59,264 --> 00:25:00,332
Well, that's...

385
00:25:01,099 --> 00:25:03,034
I want to see the Chief's divine hands.

386
00:25:03,101 --> 00:25:06,071
Don't say things like that
and mouth off in here.

387
00:25:06,137 --> 00:25:08,773
Did you forget what you said
in the conference?

388
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:10,375
Anyways, I want to be there.

389
00:25:10,675 --> 00:25:11,510
No.

390
00:25:11,576 --> 00:25:14,713
Well, have the Chief get
an MRI before the operation.

391
00:25:14,779 --> 00:25:16,214
Please have it checked.

392
00:25:16,715 --> 00:25:17,949
What are you trying to say?

393
00:25:18,850 --> 00:25:22,354
If you really want to see
the Chief operate, go observe him.

394
00:25:25,924 --> 00:25:26,758
Understood.

395
00:25:29,494 --> 00:25:30,462
What's with her?

396
00:25:33,398 --> 00:25:35,133
Chief!

397
00:25:35,467 --> 00:25:37,469
Thank you, thank you very much!

398
00:25:38,436 --> 00:25:39,271
Thank you!

399
00:25:53,018 --> 00:25:56,454
Anesthesia has spread through the body
and an epidural was given at T7/8.

400
00:25:56,788 --> 00:25:57,689
Vitals are stable.

401
00:25:57,756 --> 00:26:00,725
It's been a while, I'd like that tape.

402
00:26:00,792 --> 00:26:02,127
Oh, that one, right?

403
00:26:11,603 --> 00:26:13,605
I feel good when I listen to this.

404
00:26:14,873 --> 00:26:18,877
I used to be able to do two operations
while listening to this,

405
00:26:19,377 --> 00:26:22,614
and was able to take out
two gallstones at once.

406
00:26:22,681 --> 00:26:24,583
Of course, that's the Kubo technique.

407
00:26:27,319 --> 00:26:29,154
That's noisy, can we turn it down?

408
00:26:29,321 --> 00:26:31,990
- Well, let's start.
- Yes!

409
00:26:38,263 --> 00:26:42,100
We will perform a cholecystectomy on
Jiro Ichinose with the Chief's guidance.

410
00:26:42,167 --> 00:26:43,168
CHOLECYSTECTOMY

411
00:26:43,234 --> 00:26:45,170
- Thank you very much.
- Thank you very much.

412
00:26:46,338 --> 00:26:47,205
Scalpel.

413
00:26:52,310 --> 00:26:54,913
Hey. Who turned down the volume?

414
00:27:07,726 --> 00:27:09,661
- Please cut in this area.
- Yes.

415
00:27:09,861 --> 00:27:11,296
- Cut here.
- Yes.

416
00:27:12,597 --> 00:27:14,799
- The Chief did it.
- Yeah.

417
00:27:15,634 --> 00:27:17,469
The music is fine, hurry up.

418
00:27:21,673 --> 00:27:24,075
Oh, it's Professor Busujima!

419
00:27:24,142 --> 00:27:25,510
- Today?
- Yes.

420
00:27:26,211 --> 00:27:29,648
It's been a while,
so I thought I'd come to observe Kubo.

421
00:27:30,548 --> 00:27:33,284
Dr. Busujima and the Chief
are the same age.

422
00:27:33,418 --> 00:27:36,021
- Well, okay.
- Please sit here.

423
00:27:49,200 --> 00:27:50,702
Suction that more firmly.

424
00:27:50,802 --> 00:27:52,137
Yes. Sorry about that.

425
00:27:52,470 --> 00:27:53,905
Just relax.

426
00:27:54,939 --> 00:27:57,442
These are Kubo forceps.

427
00:27:57,509 --> 00:28:00,478
They're special forceps
with my name attached to them.

428
00:28:00,945 --> 00:28:04,382
These forceps are necessary
for the Kubo technique.

429
00:28:04,816 --> 00:28:08,219
I've done thousands
of gallstone surgeries,

430
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:11,156
but thanks to these Kubo forceps,
I was able to do

431
00:28:11,456 --> 00:28:14,759
<i>up to four surgeries in a single day.</i>

432
00:28:15,260 --> 00:28:17,462
Enough bragging, hurry up and finish.

433
00:28:27,906 --> 00:28:29,908
- Sweat.
- Excuse me.

434
00:28:30,909 --> 00:28:32,110
- Kubo forceps.
- Yes.

435
00:28:33,278 --> 00:28:34,112
Ligation.

436
00:28:34,412 --> 00:28:35,680
LIGATION
TYING BLOOD VESSELS, ETC. WITH THREAD

437
00:28:35,747 --> 00:28:37,716
- 3-0 silk, thread only.
- Yes.

438
00:28:46,758 --> 00:28:47,892
- Monopolar.
- Yes.

439
00:28:52,797 --> 00:28:55,633
Sweat's getting into my eyes.
Wipe all of it off.

440
00:28:55,967 --> 00:28:56,901
I apologize.

441
00:29:16,554 --> 00:29:18,156
Look at this gallbladder.

442
00:29:18,590 --> 00:29:22,494
Strong adhesions have formed
due to repeated inflammation.

443
00:29:22,560 --> 00:29:24,696
Abdominal section was a good choice.

444
00:29:28,933 --> 00:29:30,435
Well then, let's move on.

445
00:29:31,136 --> 00:29:32,203
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

446
00:29:36,674 --> 00:29:39,277
Blood pressure dropping.
Below 60 over immeasurable.

447
00:29:39,344 --> 00:29:41,012
Heart rate is over 150.

448
00:29:59,330 --> 00:30:02,267
- What the hell happened?
- Shock due to an unknown cause.

449
00:30:02,333 --> 00:30:04,469
Chief, what should we do?

450
00:30:07,405 --> 00:30:08,439
Chief?

451
00:30:17,749 --> 00:30:18,583
Chief?

452
00:30:23,054 --> 00:30:24,789
- Chief?
- Chief?

453
00:30:33,431 --> 00:30:34,399
Chief!

454
00:30:36,835 --> 00:30:38,703
Chief? Do you hear me?

455
00:30:38,770 --> 00:30:40,138
I'll give oxygen. Doctor.

456
00:30:41,239 --> 00:30:42,340
Tell me his condition!

457
00:30:42,407 --> 00:30:44,509
Unconscious. Left side paralysis observed.

458
00:30:44,642 --> 00:30:45,643
Get a stretcher.

459
00:30:45,710 --> 00:30:47,979
There is a possibility of a stroke.

460
00:30:48,046 --> 00:30:49,347
Contact Neurosurgery!

461
00:30:59,724 --> 00:31:02,360
Chief Kubo collapsed suddenly.
He's paralyzed on his left side.

462
00:31:02,427 --> 00:31:04,295
- Clear the way! Bring me the IV!
- Yes.

463
00:31:14,305 --> 00:31:15,740
Chief, we're moving you.

464
00:31:24,048 --> 00:31:25,550
CT now! Transport him quickly!

465
00:31:25,650 --> 00:31:27,352
Watch out. Be careful.

466
00:31:31,389 --> 00:31:32,557
Someone stay behind!

467
00:31:53,177 --> 00:31:54,445
I'll continue the operation.

468
00:31:57,248 --> 00:31:58,549
Huh? You?

469
00:32:03,655 --> 00:32:04,489
Scalpel.

470
00:32:05,657 --> 00:32:06,491
Yes.

471
00:32:17,568 --> 00:32:19,971
Wait! Continuing like this is dangerous.

472
00:32:36,621 --> 00:32:37,822
Daimon?

473
00:32:37,889 --> 00:32:39,991
You, the anesthesiologist. Vitals.

474
00:32:40,758 --> 00:32:43,795
Blood pressure is below 60
over immeasurable. Heart rate 170.

475
00:32:44,262 --> 00:32:45,263
You, assistant.

476
00:32:46,431 --> 00:32:48,466
It's just you here,
so you're the first assistant.

477
00:32:48,933 --> 00:32:52,470
I'll do it. Professor appointed me
as his first assistant.

478
00:32:52,704 --> 00:32:55,139
I'll continue the operation. I'll do it!

479
00:32:55,206 --> 00:32:56,307
Don't touch him!

480
00:32:56,975 --> 00:32:59,444
Don't touch him with those gloves.
Everyone, hold up!

481
00:33:03,715 --> 00:33:05,483
Ventilate the room as much as possible.

482
00:33:05,850 --> 00:33:06,985
- Hurry!
- Yes.

483
00:33:07,652 --> 00:33:09,754
Anesthesiologist,
take one ampule epinephrine.

484
00:33:10,288 --> 00:33:11,923
Administer it in the trachea
from the tube.

485
00:33:15,660 --> 00:33:17,061
They're late. Where are they?

486
00:33:29,273 --> 00:33:31,009
Everyone change their gloves.

487
00:33:31,476 --> 00:33:32,310
Hurry!

488
00:33:33,811 --> 00:33:34,712
You too.

489
00:33:39,617 --> 00:33:41,452
Administer steroid
with an IV when you finish.

490
00:33:48,326 --> 00:33:49,394
Move!

491
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:51,329
Chief!

492
00:33:51,496 --> 00:33:54,399
- Easy, take it easy.
- Director, hang in there!

493
00:34:02,740 --> 00:34:03,641
It stopped?

494
00:34:04,809 --> 00:34:08,179
Blood pressure is 120 over 65.
Heart rate 90.

495
00:34:08,246 --> 00:34:09,947
All right. Let's restart the operation.

496
00:34:10,415 --> 00:34:12,650
First, detach the adhesions.
Metzenbaum scissors.

497
00:34:12,717 --> 00:34:13,551
Yes.

498
00:34:46,851 --> 00:34:49,087
Let's remove the gallbladder.
Mosquito Pean.

499
00:34:49,153 --> 00:34:50,421
- Forceps
- Yes.

500
00:34:59,197 --> 00:35:00,465
So fast.

501
00:35:00,631 --> 00:35:02,834
- Bile duct ligation.
- Oh, yes.

502
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:04,735
Hand me
the fine-tip Pean forceps. 3/0 silk.

503
00:35:09,807 --> 00:35:11,476
- Tie it tighter.
- Yes.

504
00:35:17,181 --> 00:35:20,017
- Triple ligature.
- Understood.

505
00:35:20,485 --> 00:35:21,919
Removing the gallbladder.
Metzenbaum scissors.

506
00:35:22,386 --> 00:35:23,221
Yes.

507
00:35:34,232 --> 00:35:35,500
- Send it to the lab.
- Yes.

508
00:35:35,600 --> 00:35:37,969
- How's the gauze count?
- It's okay.

509
00:35:38,035 --> 00:35:41,472
We will proceed to abdominal closure.
3/0 absorbable suture.

510
00:35:55,520 --> 00:35:57,655
- Blood loss amount is?
- 200cc.

511
00:35:57,722 --> 00:36:00,391
- Before the patient wakes up--
- I'll administer 100ml of steroid.

512
00:36:01,993 --> 00:36:03,261
Okay, we're finished.

513
00:36:13,504 --> 00:36:14,338
Doctor.

514
00:36:16,807 --> 00:36:18,476
Thanks for your hard work.

515
00:36:30,188 --> 00:36:34,192
Oh, Professor Busujima!
Are you still here?

516
00:36:34,792 --> 00:36:37,862
For a while, we weren't sure
about the Chief,

517
00:36:39,096 --> 00:36:41,933
but we have
an excellent Neurosurgery department.

518
00:36:44,035 --> 00:36:46,504
- Who is that woman?
- Huh?

519
00:37:35,820 --> 00:37:37,221
You're late. Where were you?

520
00:37:37,355 --> 00:37:39,523
She was nonchalantly
eating noodles in the cafeteria.

521
00:37:39,724 --> 00:37:41,092
I hadn't had lunch yet.

522
00:37:42,093 --> 00:37:43,961
Give us an operation report before lunch.

523
00:37:45,630 --> 00:37:48,065
Why did you operate even though
you weren't the primary surgeon?

524
00:37:48,132 --> 00:37:50,067
You'd rather the patient die?

525
00:37:50,134 --> 00:37:51,302
Answer the question.

526
00:37:53,371 --> 00:37:54,939
The operating surgeon collapsed.

527
00:37:55,006 --> 00:37:57,308
Only the assistant and anesthesiologist
were there, so I did it.

528
00:37:57,375 --> 00:38:01,545
Operating without permission
is unthinkable. This is no field hospital.

529
00:38:01,812 --> 00:38:02,913
- Morimoto.
- Yes.

530
00:38:03,247 --> 00:38:07,351
Why did you not continue the operation
as the primary assistant?

531
00:38:09,053 --> 00:38:10,454
I was planning to,

532
00:38:11,856 --> 00:38:12,990
but she kicked me.

533
00:38:13,324 --> 00:38:16,027
- What?
- No, I'm very sorry!

534
00:38:17,795 --> 00:38:20,231
The patient's condition changed suddenly.

535
00:38:20,431 --> 00:38:22,566
Dr. Morimoto was shaken too, so...

536
00:38:22,633 --> 00:38:23,701
Sudden change?

537
00:38:23,768 --> 00:38:27,638
The patient was in
an acute state of shock.

538
00:38:27,738 --> 00:38:30,041
The heart rate was over 150.

539
00:38:30,508 --> 00:38:31,909
- Cause?
- Unknown.

540
00:38:32,610 --> 00:38:33,944
I don't know either.

541
00:38:36,714 --> 00:38:37,615
The cause?

542
00:38:39,784 --> 00:38:43,521
The Professor, you, you,
and all of you have medical licenses.

543
00:38:43,921 --> 00:38:46,123
How about you diagnose it yourselves?

544
00:38:49,660 --> 00:38:52,563
Well, if you'll excuse me,
I am starving.

545
00:38:52,897 --> 00:38:55,199
Hey, wait. Stop kidding around.

546
00:38:58,602 --> 00:39:00,604
May I intrude?

547
00:39:00,871 --> 00:39:01,772
What is it, Kaji?

548
00:39:02,840 --> 00:39:04,208
Michiko Daimon.

549
00:39:04,775 --> 00:39:07,378
You... are quite suspicious.

550
00:39:08,479 --> 00:39:09,313
What's wrong?

551
00:39:09,647 --> 00:39:14,118
This morning, she was speaking quickly
with the medical equipment salesman,

552
00:39:14,185 --> 00:39:15,553
so I did some checking.

553
00:39:15,920 --> 00:39:19,557
I found out that she ordered
the gloves on her own.

554
00:39:19,657 --> 00:39:22,426
- What?
- Ten boxes of surgical gloves.

555
00:39:23,027 --> 00:39:26,497
Why would you do that? Do you know
how much a pair of those costs?

556
00:39:26,964 --> 00:39:29,133
- Is it true?
- I was in a hurry.

557
00:39:29,834 --> 00:39:32,136
I wonder, why were you in such a hurry?

558
00:39:33,904 --> 00:39:38,008
If you didn't get found out,
were you planning to resell them?

559
00:39:38,476 --> 00:39:40,411
- Resell...
- Wait a minute!

560
00:39:40,478 --> 00:39:42,146
What's this about gloves?

561
00:39:45,716 --> 00:39:46,751
Well, Daimon?

562
00:39:47,685 --> 00:39:49,687
Hey, what are you looking at?

563
00:39:51,122 --> 00:39:52,289
Answer me!

564
00:39:56,260 --> 00:39:58,129
It's time. Please excuse me.

565
00:40:04,535 --> 00:40:06,937
I... I am really very sorry.

566
00:40:09,340 --> 00:40:10,207
See?

567
00:40:11,108 --> 00:40:13,411
You shouldn't trust a freelance doctor.

568
00:40:14,745 --> 00:40:18,949
She was planning to resell the gloves
if she wasn't found out.

569
00:40:20,084 --> 00:40:22,520
By the way, I think she left
Totei University's Medical Office

570
00:40:22,586 --> 00:40:24,021
under shady circumstances, too.

571
00:40:24,388 --> 00:40:26,223
- Money or a medical error.
- Huh?

572
00:40:26,290 --> 00:40:28,259
So she was a shady doctor to begin with.

573
00:40:28,325 --> 00:40:31,462
Then there's one more big question.

574
00:40:33,030 --> 00:40:35,699
How did that woman know
that the Director

575
00:40:36,500 --> 00:40:40,604
was about to have a stroke?

576
00:40:43,774 --> 00:40:45,810
Now that you say it,
before the surgery,

577
00:40:45,910 --> 00:40:49,213
didn't she say the Director should get
an MRI and have Neurosurgery check him?

578
00:41:00,157 --> 00:41:00,991
Father.

579
00:41:10,601 --> 00:41:12,736
- Doctor.
- He's recovering well.

580
00:41:13,137 --> 00:41:15,172
He should be able
to start  walking tomorrow.

581
00:41:15,239 --> 00:41:17,408
Thank you! Um...

582
00:41:18,142 --> 00:41:22,112
We'd like to thank the Chief
who performed the surgery.

583
00:41:23,180 --> 00:41:25,616
He collapsed and is resting.
You can't see him today.

584
00:41:26,617 --> 00:41:30,387
No smoking for two to three days.
Wait until the phlegm clears up.

585
00:41:42,733 --> 00:41:44,068
I'm hungry.

586
00:41:56,146 --> 00:41:58,816
According to the tests,
there's no need for surgery.

587
00:41:59,049 --> 00:42:00,217
We're all relieved.

588
00:42:01,151 --> 00:42:05,155
We were worried to death yesterday. Right?

589
00:42:07,925 --> 00:42:08,759
Yes?

590
00:42:10,094 --> 00:42:11,996
How was the operation?

591
00:42:12,062 --> 00:42:13,264
Please don't worry. 

592
00:42:13,330 --> 00:42:16,433
The surgery was a great success
and the patient is recovering nicely.

593
00:42:17,635 --> 00:42:21,105
Who did the operation?

594
00:42:23,007 --> 00:42:26,176
In my place...

595
00:42:27,678 --> 00:42:30,548
Morimoto?

596
00:42:33,017 --> 00:42:34,885
Hara?

597
00:42:48,599 --> 00:42:50,067
I've brought Dr. Daimon.

598
00:42:56,707 --> 00:42:58,776
He's asking if you did the surgery.

599
00:42:59,743 --> 00:43:00,611
Yes, I did.

600
00:43:04,748 --> 00:43:06,150
He says thanks for your hard work.

601
00:43:07,685 --> 00:43:08,519
Thank you.

602
00:43:13,991 --> 00:43:16,594
He says the Kubo method
was the right choice.

603
00:43:18,963 --> 00:43:22,566
No. I still think we should have
avoided open stomach surgery.

604
00:43:23,400 --> 00:43:24,234
Daimon!

605
00:43:25,436 --> 00:43:28,672
Is there anything else?
If not, please excuse me.

606
00:43:30,174 --> 00:43:31,008
Wait.

607
00:43:35,846 --> 00:43:37,114
He says you're fired.

608
00:43:56,500 --> 00:43:57,568
Daimon.

609
00:44:04,541 --> 00:44:06,977
I was fired, so excuse me.

610
00:44:14,852 --> 00:44:18,422
MICHIKO DAIMON

611
00:44:34,204 --> 00:44:37,107
Of course she was going to be fired.

612
00:44:38,876 --> 00:44:43,380
She mouthed off
at the Director as a new hire,

613
00:44:43,447 --> 00:44:45,983
and she ordered gloves
to resell on her own.

614
00:44:46,316 --> 00:44:49,086
Now that she's fired,
it'll finally be peaceful.

615
00:44:49,319 --> 00:44:51,789
But, she was a really good surgeon.

616
00:44:56,560 --> 00:45:00,230
Shouldn't we check and make sure
nothing's missing around here?

617
00:45:04,134 --> 00:45:06,970
Does no one understand
the meaning of the gloves?

618
00:45:08,272 --> 00:45:09,239
What about the gloves?

619
00:45:10,174 --> 00:45:12,076
I don't know about the gloves,

620
00:45:12,142 --> 00:45:14,645
but she made all of us change them
during the operation.

621
00:45:15,579 --> 00:45:16,880
- Gloves?
- Yes.

622
00:45:16,947 --> 00:45:20,017
Don't touch him with those gloves!
Everyone, hold up!

623
00:45:21,385 --> 00:45:24,655
No way...
That patient has a latex allergy?

624
00:45:24,722 --> 00:45:27,291
Blood pressure dropping.
Below 60 over immeasurable.

625
00:45:27,357 --> 00:45:29,059
Heart rate is over 150.

626
00:45:29,126 --> 00:45:31,895
He probably suffered
an anaphylaxis attack.

627
00:45:32,129 --> 00:45:33,097
May I?

628
00:45:33,163 --> 00:45:36,266
ANAPHYLAXIS ATTACK
A POTENTIALLY FATAL ALLERGIC REACTION

629
00:45:37,234 --> 00:45:39,002
The gloves she ordered

630
00:45:39,069 --> 00:45:41,438
are completely latex-free.

631
00:45:41,505 --> 00:45:44,308
The gloves we always use
in our hospital are...

632
00:45:44,374 --> 00:45:45,542
SONOKO CHIBA
CHIEF NURSE

633
00:45:45,642 --> 00:45:47,878
...made of latex.

634
00:45:51,582 --> 00:45:53,584
No, that's not possible.

635
00:45:55,018 --> 00:45:58,989
How could she predict
the anaphylaxis attack before the surgery?

636
00:46:01,091 --> 00:46:04,294
Come to think of it,
the patient runs a rubber factory.

637
00:46:04,361 --> 00:46:08,665
Latex allergies are more likely to develop
with those who handle rubber a long time.

638
00:46:08,732 --> 00:46:11,502
It's coincidence.
How could she have imagined that?

639
00:46:11,568 --> 00:46:15,239
But even then,
she was the only one able to remain calm.

640
00:46:18,776 --> 00:46:21,879
If she wasn't there, no one would have
been able to save the patient.

641
00:46:27,951 --> 00:46:29,753
Where did Dr. Daimon go?

642
00:46:31,455 --> 00:46:32,523
She was fired.

643
00:46:33,090 --> 00:46:34,858
- What?
- Enough about that.

644
00:46:34,925 --> 00:46:36,693
Everyone get back to work.

645
00:46:42,266 --> 00:46:44,034
She's not that kind of person.

646
00:46:45,235 --> 00:46:47,671
She's definitely not that kind of person.

647
00:46:48,071 --> 00:46:49,807
Dr. Kaji, what else is wrong?

648
00:46:50,607 --> 00:46:53,944
How did she know that
the Chief would have a stroke?

649
00:46:54,178 --> 00:46:55,779
Well, there's that, but...

650
00:46:57,080 --> 00:46:59,683
She must have drugged him or something.

651
00:47:00,050 --> 00:47:00,884
What?

652
00:47:02,186 --> 00:47:06,190
She's not Daimon. She's a demon.

653
00:47:16,633 --> 00:47:18,435
Michiko... <i>Ron.</i>

654
00:47:18,569 --> 00:47:20,737
- What?
<i>- Haneman.</i>

655
00:47:21,605 --> 00:47:24,441
Ah, I lost again!

656
00:47:24,508 --> 00:47:28,579
You may be a good surgeon,
but as usual you're a bad mah-jong player.

657
00:47:28,679 --> 00:47:32,349
Let's play one more time! I have
to recover my loss from my lost job.

658
00:47:32,416 --> 00:47:33,717
You got fired again?

659
00:47:33,784 --> 00:47:36,553
Falling deeper and deeper into debt...

660
00:47:37,888 --> 00:47:40,424
a living hell mired in debt.

661
00:47:54,238 --> 00:47:59,443
I heard the Director collapsed
during surgery.

662
00:48:00,210 --> 00:48:01,311
Is that true?

663
00:48:03,280 --> 00:48:05,515
Ah... yes.

664
00:48:06,216 --> 00:48:09,052
But he's stable now,
so there's no need to worry.

665
00:48:11,188 --> 00:48:12,289
That's good.

666
00:48:14,791 --> 00:48:19,897
Professor Kubo performed surgery on you
at the risk of his own life.

667
00:48:21,465 --> 00:48:23,066
We're blessed, aren't we?

668
00:48:23,901 --> 00:48:26,036
It's all thanks to his divine hands.

669
00:48:26,103 --> 00:48:27,371
It really is.

670
00:48:53,931 --> 00:48:55,165
Dr. Daimon!

671
00:48:57,167 --> 00:48:58,669
Your surgery was amazing.

672
00:48:59,603 --> 00:49:03,974
Antibodies against latex were found
in Mr. Ichinose's blood.

673
00:49:05,475 --> 00:49:09,313
If you weren't there, we don't know
what would've happened to him.

674
00:49:11,548 --> 00:49:14,151
Um... why didn't you tell
the hospital that?

675
00:49:14,551 --> 00:49:15,619
A shot of tequila.

676
00:49:17,087 --> 00:49:18,488
You won't have to quit.

677
00:49:19,156 --> 00:49:21,658
The Chief will accept that you were right.

678
00:49:24,761 --> 00:49:27,331
- I consider that a huge pain.
- What?

679
00:49:28,231 --> 00:49:29,199
Who are you anyway?

680
00:49:32,169 --> 00:49:33,003
Move.

681
00:49:49,920 --> 00:49:51,421
That's definitely Dr. Daimon.

682
00:50:00,597 --> 00:50:02,899
- Is he out of danger now?
- Yes.

683
00:50:04,067 --> 00:50:05,702
It's good the medication is working.

684
00:50:07,137 --> 00:50:08,739
But there's still physical therapy,

685
00:50:10,440 --> 00:50:13,443
and he can't continue
as Hospital Chief, right?

686
00:50:17,014 --> 00:50:17,848
Professor,

687
00:50:19,249 --> 00:50:20,617
we have hopes for you.

688
00:50:21,952 --> 00:50:23,653
Our next Hospital Chief.

689
00:50:31,395 --> 00:50:34,197
So this is it for Kubo.

690
00:50:36,967 --> 00:50:40,670
It's unfortunate he never got to return
to the main campus.

691
00:50:40,737 --> 00:50:45,208
About the next chief
of the Third Hospital...

692
00:50:48,745 --> 00:50:50,347
Isn't it Torii?

693
00:50:59,089 --> 00:51:01,091
- One more.
- Certainly.

694
00:51:28,552 --> 00:51:31,054
- Thank you very much.
- Thank you very much.

695
00:51:33,156 --> 00:51:34,157
I'm very sorry.

696
00:51:44,968 --> 00:51:47,904
<i>From now, the new Chief,</i>
<i>Professor Busujima,</i>

697
00:51:47,971 --> 00:51:50,874
<i>will now make the rounds.</i>

698
00:52:04,054 --> 00:52:06,323
CHIEF'S ROOM

699
00:52:12,195 --> 00:52:13,964
Thank you for waiting.

700
00:52:21,304 --> 00:52:25,008
Professor Busujima, congratulations
on your appointment as Hospital Chief.

701
00:52:25,108 --> 00:52:27,777
No, it's like being exiled
from the capital.

702
00:52:28,178 --> 00:52:29,579
You're joking again.

703
00:52:31,314 --> 00:52:34,918
Manager, have you finished
Daimon's contract?

704
00:52:34,985 --> 00:52:37,487
Yes. I hurried to bring it here.

705
00:52:42,359 --> 00:52:43,727
DOCTOR HIRE CONTRACT

706
00:52:43,793 --> 00:52:49,166
Thank you again
for designating our Michiko Daimon.

707
00:52:49,232 --> 00:52:52,235
Then this concludes the contract.
Thank you.

708
00:52:52,302 --> 00:52:53,703
Please wait a minute.

709
00:52:54,471 --> 00:52:56,873
Allow me to state our terms.

710
00:52:58,408 --> 00:52:59,543
Pardon me.

711
00:53:05,348 --> 00:53:09,219
First of all, working hours shall be
from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.

712
00:53:09,286 --> 00:53:14,891
Eight hours of work a day,
with one hour for lunch within that.

713
00:53:15,125 --> 00:53:17,661
Anything over that
will incur extra charges.

714
00:53:18,094 --> 00:53:19,763
This is the list of charges.

715
00:53:22,299 --> 00:53:26,303
As you can see, work outside
of regular hours is 30,000 yen per hour,

716
00:53:26,536 --> 00:53:29,573
and emergency operations
not in the contract are 300,000 yen.

717
00:53:30,240 --> 00:53:32,108
That'll cost us more
than my annual salary!

718
00:53:33,009 --> 00:53:35,512
- Really?
- There's no way we'll recognize that.

719
00:53:35,579 --> 00:53:38,748
Would you like to register
with our agency as well?

720
00:53:39,082 --> 00:53:39,983
Don't joke!

721
00:53:40,684 --> 00:53:43,720
As it is, I can't be responsible
for a freelance surgeon.

722
00:53:44,354 --> 00:53:46,189
What will you do if you make a mistake?

723
00:53:46,790 --> 00:53:48,024
Don't worry.

724
00:53:50,393 --> 00:53:52,195
I never fail.

725
00:53:58,201 --> 00:54:01,137
Mr. Akira, my most important term.

726
00:54:01,371 --> 00:54:02,205
Yes.

727
00:54:02,772 --> 00:54:05,709
We need you to strictly follow this term.

728
00:54:07,010 --> 00:54:10,280
I will not do any work
that doesn't require a medical license.

729
00:54:10,513 --> 00:54:12,515
What the... Wait a minute!

730
00:54:12,716 --> 00:54:15,819
University Hospital medical staff
have a lot of miscellaneous work to do!

731
00:54:15,885 --> 00:54:19,990
Understood. "For example:
Help a professor with his research.

732
00:54:20,056 --> 00:54:21,157
I won't.

733
00:54:21,224 --> 00:54:22,459
Research for essays.

734
00:54:22,525 --> 00:54:23,360
I won't.

735
00:54:23,426 --> 00:54:25,095
Director's and Professor's rounds.

736
00:54:25,161 --> 00:54:26,129
I won't.

737
00:54:26,196 --> 00:54:27,130
Accompany at academic conferences.

738
00:54:27,197 --> 00:54:28,265
I won't.

739
00:54:28,331 --> 00:54:29,466
Take professors to and from golf courses.

740
00:54:29,532 --> 00:54:30,500
I won't.

741
00:54:30,600 --> 00:54:31,968
Scheme to cover up a mistress.

742
00:54:32,035 --> 00:54:33,069
I won't.

743
00:54:33,136 --> 00:54:35,538
Attend drinking parties and so on."

744
00:54:35,839 --> 00:54:37,607
It's written here in detail.

745
00:54:40,910 --> 00:54:43,013
I will do none of those items.

746
00:54:45,048 --> 00:54:45,915
That's it.

747
00:54:49,919 --> 00:54:51,421
- Turn it down.
- Why?

748
00:54:51,488 --> 00:54:54,457
- Professor Torii is right.
- I agree.

749
00:55:07,370 --> 00:55:08,371
Understood.

750
00:55:08,938 --> 00:55:10,940
We'll have you start today.

751
00:55:14,110 --> 00:55:16,613
Then that settles it. Thank you very much.

752
00:55:18,315 --> 00:55:19,783
Michiko Daimon.

753
00:55:32,228 --> 00:55:35,632
A medical license isn't required
for that, is it?

754
00:55:38,968 --> 00:55:39,803
Later.

755
00:55:43,306 --> 00:55:44,407
VISITOR

756
00:55:57,520 --> 00:55:59,522
<i>Chief, why did you hire her?</i>

757
00:56:00,757 --> 00:56:03,159
She has an amazing background, no?

758
00:56:04,694 --> 00:56:07,764
<i>She hates groups, she hates authority,</i>

759
00:56:08,264 --> 00:56:09,799
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

760
00:56:10,400 --> 00:56:16,139
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

761
00:56:32,021 --> 00:56:33,690
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

762
00:56:36,059 --> 00:56:37,060
<i>Also known as...</i>

763
00:56:39,095 --> 00:56:40,463
<i>Doctor X.</i>

764
00:58:06,850 --> 00:58:09,152
Subtitle translation by Paul Koehler

765
00:58:09,319 --> 00:58:10,987
This drama is fiction. All names of people
and organizations are fictional.

766
00:58:11,054 --> 00:58:12,655
Medical practices in the drama vary
depending on a person's medical condition.

767
00:58:12,722 --> 00:58:13,590
PREVIEW
YOU CAN BUY THAT ARM WITH MONEY

768
00:58:13,656 --> 00:58:14,791
It's okay not to fail, right?

769
00:58:14,858 --> 00:58:16,359
<i>Her goal is to get money from VIPs.</i>

770
00:58:16,426 --> 00:58:18,495
<i>It's my rule to get 100,000 yen.</i>

771
00:58:18,561 --> 00:58:19,963
You're mistaken!

772
00:58:20,096 --> 00:58:22,699
<i>As a doctor and as a human,</i>
<i>you're the worst!</i>

773
00:58:23,099 --> 00:58:25,034
Do the operation until the very end!

774
00:58:25,101 --> 00:58:25,935
WHAT ARE LIFE'S PRIORITIES?

775
00:58:26,002 --> 00:58:27,637
I will not fail.
